Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `borough`: filter to records that occurred in the Westminster local authority area.  
• `major_category`: filter to the high‑level offence group “Theft and Handling”.  
• `minor_category`: filter to the specific sub‑type “Other Theft”.  
• `year`: used to break the results down by calendar year.  
• `value`: the count of offences for that row – to be summed for yearly totals.  

Typical filter conditions that will appear  
```
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
  AND major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
  AND minor_category = 'Other Theft'
```

Ten progressively more‑complex exploratory queries (all capped at 20 rows with DISTINCT or LIMIT where appropriate):

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a few raw Westminster rows in the crime table
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List distinct major offence groups for Westminster
SELECT DISTINCT major_category
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show distinct minor categories inside “Theft and Handling”
SELECT DISTINCT minor_category
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
  AND borough = 'Westminster'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Sample the monthly crime counts for “Other Theft” in 2015
SELECT lsoa_code, year, month, value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
  AND major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
  AND minor_category = 'Other Theft'
  AND year = 2015
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Verify that the numeric counts are positive / reasonable
SELECT value, COUNT(*) AS row_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
  AND major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
  AND minor_category = 'Other Theft'
GROUP BY value
ORDER BY value DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Calculate the total “Other Theft” for a single year (example 2012)
SELECT SUM(value) AS other_theft_2012
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
  AND major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
  AND minor_category = 'Other Theft'
  AND year = 2012;
```

```sql
-- 7. Retrieve yearly totals for the borough, all minor categories
SELECT year, minor_category, SUM(value) AS tot_crimes
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
GROUP BY year, minor_category
ORDER BY year, minor_category
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Yearly totals within “Theft and Handling” across all of London
SELECT year, borough, SUM(value) AS london_theft_handling
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
GROUP BY year, borough
ORDER BY year, borough
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Compare Westminster with another borough for “Other Theft”
SELECT year,
       SUM(CASE WHEN borough = 'Westminster' THEN value END) AS westminster_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN borough = 'Camden'      THEN value END) AS camden_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
  AND minor_category = 'Other Theft'
  AND borough IN ('Westminster', 'Camden')
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER QUERY:
--    Total number of “Other Theft” incidents in the “Theft and Handling” category
--    for each year, restricted to the borough of Westminster
SELECT
  year,
  SUM(value) AS total_other_theft_incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Westminster'
  AND major_category = 'Theft and Handling'
  AND minor_category = 'Other Theft'
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year;
```
